:IMHELP name='DUPMSGD/REPLACE   '.
:EHELP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für den Befehl
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='DUPMSGD'.
Duplicate Message Description (DUPMSGD) - Help
:P.
The DUPMSGD command is used to duplicate a message description. The
DUPMSGD command carries over lots of parameters of a message
description but unfortunately it can not carry over all parameters
due to the restriction of the API used.
:P.
The following parameters are carried over:
:P.
:LINES.
- Message text                 (parameter MSG)
- Second level text            (parameter SECLVL)
- Severity                     (parameter SEV)
- Message data fields          (parameter FMT)
- Alert options                (parameter ALROPT)
- Default reply value          (parameter DFT)
- Log problem                  (parameter LOGPRB)
- Coded character set ID       (parameter CCSID)
:ELINES.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort RANGE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DUPMSGD/RANGE     '.
Range of message identifiers - Help
:XH3.Range of message identifiers (RANGE)
:P.
Specifies the range of message identifiers in the
specified message file which are processed by the command. All
message descriptions in the message file specified on the
:HP2.Message:EHP2. file prompt (MSGF parameter) can be processed
by specifying *ALL on this parameter.
:P.
If the starting message identifier is not specified, the
message descriptions begin with the first message in the
specified message file.  If the ending message identifier
is not specified, the default value, *ONLY, is used, and
only the description of the starting message identifier is
processed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:XH3.Starting Message Identifier
:P.
The first of the two values in this parameter, called the
starting message identifier, specifies the message
identifier of the first message description to be processed.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first message in the file specified on the :HP2.Message
file:EHP2. prompt (MSGF parameter) is the first message
whose description is processed.
:PT.:PV.lower-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the 7-character identifier of the first
message description to be processed.
:EPARML.
:P.
:XH3.Ending Message Identifier
:P.
The second of the two values, called the ending message
identifier, specifies the message identifier for the last
message description to be processed.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.Only the message identifier specified as a starting
message identifier is processed.
:PT.:PV.*LAST:EPV.
:PD.The last message in the file is the last message whose
description is processed.
:PT.:PV.upper-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the 7-character identifier of the last message
description to be processed.
:EPARML.
:P.
:XH3.Other Single Values:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.*ALL:EPV.
:PD.All message descriptions in the message file specified
are processed.  This value can only be specified in the first
element of this parameter.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort FROMMSGF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DUPMSGD/FROMMSGF'.
From message file - Help
:XH3.From message file (FROMMSGF)
:P.
Specifies the name an library of the source message file.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QCPFMSG:EPK.
:PD.Message descriptions are taken from the system message
file, QCPFMSG.
:PT.:PV.source-message-file-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the message file from which the
message descriptions are taken.
:EPARML.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched
until the first match is found.
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the
message file.  If no current library entry exists in
the library list, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the library where the message file is located.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort TOMSGID
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DUPMSGD/TOMSGID'.
To message description - Help
:XH3.To message description (TOMSGID)
:P.
Specifies the target message identifier. The source message description is
added with that message identifier to the target message file.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FROMID:EPK.
:PD.The new message description gets the same identifier as the old
message description. *FROMID can only be specified, if
:HP2.To message file:EHP2. (parameter TOMSGF) is set to a value
other than *FROMMSGF.
:PT.:PV.target-message-identifier:EPV.
:PD.Specify the message identifier that is used for the target
message description.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort TOMSGF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DUPMSGD/TOMSGF'.
To message file - Help
:XH3.To message file (TOMSGF)
:P.
Specifies the name an library of the target message file.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FROMMSGF:EPK.
:PD.The target messsage file is the message file specified
on the :HP2.From message file:EHP2. (parameter FROMMSGF) parameter.
:PT.:PV.target-message-file-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the message file to that the message
descriptions are added.
:EPARML.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched
until the first match is found.
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the
message file.  If no current library entry exists in
the library list, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the library where the message file is located.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort REPLACE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='DUPMSGD/REPLACE'.
Replace message description - Help
:XH3.Replace message description (REPLACE)
:P.
Specifies whether an existing message description is allowed to be
replaced or not.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.An existing message description is not replaced. An error message
is issued by the command instead.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.An exisiting message description is replaced  by the message
description duplicated.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
